===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who [[consume]]s no [[animal]] [[flesh]] with the [[exception]] of [[fish#Noun|fish]] or [[seafood]]. {{defdate|c. 1990}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|author=Jessica R. Shawl|title=‘Vegetarians’???|url=https://groups.google.com/d/msg/rec.food.veg/7RRDmHNgT90/f3k23qtV8nUJ|newsgroup=rec.food.veg|id=36FBD2DB.8237C15@scdt.intel.com|date=26 March 1999|passage=I'm curious what you do when you encounter a friend, family member, whoever who claims to be a "vegetarian who eats fish". It *really* bothers me when this happens because it contributes to the assumption that I eat fish and I don't, because I am a vegetarian. I feel like it gives all vegetarians a bad name. Do you correct them? Do you not bother? And how do you correct them? I was thinking that saying something like "oh, you mean your{{sic}} a '''pescetarian'''" would be ok and give them the appropriate term. Speaking of which, how is "'''pescetarian'''" pronounced?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Pierre Jean Cousin|author2=Kirsten Hartvig|title=The Complete Guide to Nutritional Health: More Than 600 Foods and Recipes for Overcoming Illness and Boosting your Immunity|location=London|publisher=Duncan Baird Publishers|year=2004|page=149|isbn=978-1-84483-115-9|passage=Eat for Immunity follows a plant-based approach to improving immunity that is relevant to every style of eating—carnivore, '''pescetarian''', vegetarian and vegan.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Ayun Halliday|authorlink=Ayun Halliday|title=Dirty Sugar Cookies: Culinary Observations, Questionable Taste|location=Emeryville, Calif.|publisher=[[w:Perseus Books Group|Seal Press]]|year=2006|page=151|isbn=978-1-58005-150-7|passage="Why don't you just tell people you're a '''pescetarian'''?" a vegetarian I met recently asked, cutting me off midapologia for my beat-up leather jacket and my callow habit of behaving as if fish are neurologically no more complex than eggplants.}}

